WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Erica Wernick: Everything that&nbsp;
we say we want is because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.880
how we think we're going to feel when we get it...

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.960
Film Courage: How do you define success?

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.960
Erica: My definition of success has changed&nbsp;
over the last two years and I would not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.880
be surprised if it changed again in&nbsp;
the next coming years. I think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:28.000
for the last 10 years I really define success&nbsp;
by the projects I was booking and the money I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:37.920
was making and once I got those things that&nbsp;
I desired then I realized wait a minute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.840
I really just want to be happy (not that some&nbsp;
of those things didn't make me happy) but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:52.480
now I'm really chasing for lack of a&nbsp;
better word what makes me happy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:01:00.720
and that's to me more important i think that i'm&nbsp;
still weaving into my you know one of my coaches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.600
was like oh so you say that's what or maybe my&nbsp;
therapist said this you say that success is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.760
about what makes you happy but you're still&nbsp;
kind of living in this world where you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.560
to make a certain amount of money and you want&nbsp;
to book certain projects and and so i think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.960
i have one foot in that world and one foot in&nbsp;
this world but for me it's so much more about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.680
being happy and helping people&nbsp;
and so i'm i'm trying to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:34.400
refocus my energy on that because i think it's&nbsp;
really easy to get caught up especially in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.120
social media world where we're comparing ourselves&nbsp;
to other people all the time and what their lives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.560
look like and where they're spending their money&nbsp;
and what projects you know i think um you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.560
a lot of my actor clients we talk about how their&nbsp;
least favorite question ever is have i seen you in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:56.640
anything or are you working on anything now people&nbsp;
feel very insecure about that question and so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.800
i just you know i myself have gotten very&nbsp;
caught up in what projects i'm working on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:10.320
so that i can tell other people and then i&nbsp;
will be perceived as successful and being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:16.240
perceived as successful is more important than&nbsp;
how i actually feel doing these things and so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:25.040
um so now i'm just trying to let go of that and&nbsp;
focus on what makes me happy like i think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.320
you know it's like if we look back at&nbsp;
our lives i don't know i would rather be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.080
happy and doing things that feel good&nbsp;
and excite me than constantly worrying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.320
about trying to compare myself to others&nbsp;
and what it looks like to other people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.200
what do you think about the fact that that's&nbsp;
a great place to be in but some people might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:54.000
need to have kissed the ring so to speak and then&nbsp;
realize you know what it wasn't that great and i&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.160
actually just want to be happy but they needed&nbsp;
that experience to know i actually was up here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:07.520
for a little bit and i decided i wasn't happy but&nbsp;
i needed to know what that felt like yeah i think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:13.840
that we all are on our own journey we all are on&nbsp;
our own path you know if i had to experience that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.120
to learn this lesson it's not even necessarily&nbsp;
a lesson it's just a redirect for myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:25.760
um and so i don't think there's anything wrong&nbsp;
with like some people just have to live out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.960
their journey and live out their own experiences&nbsp;
than to decide what they want you know i think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:35.760
that's what we're always collecting data based&nbsp;
on how we feel so everything that we do we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.160
collecting data and then we're re-evaluating&nbsp;
so i think that's totally okay but what i do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.800
sort of direct people in my book is to and&nbsp;
again this is something that i feel like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:53.600
that i've been working on is to stop setting&nbsp;
goals that are based on validation right so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.920
try to at least start chasing the joy because i&nbsp;
think that the all those things that you think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.280
you want they're going to come anyway right you&nbsp;
can be happy and get all those things but we don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.840
necessarily always know why we want those things&nbsp;
and so i think it is important to take a look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:15.840
like well why do i want that you know like i&nbsp;
remember i have a dream of buying a house it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.400
used to be in the hills but now i want one in the&nbsp;
palisades or you know with ocean view as opposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.880
to city view and i remember someone said to me&nbsp;
oh do you want that because of how it'll look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:31.440
and i said oh my gosh no that that's not part of&nbsp;
this dream for me at all i want it because i have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.000
family back on the east coast and i want rooms&nbsp;
for them to come visit for extended periods of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.400
time so that i can be you know i'm very close&nbsp;
with my family and i hate that they're so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:46.000
away and i don't get to see them very often um and&nbsp;
i'm also very sensitive to my surroundings that i&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:51.200
want surroundings that inspire me and excite&nbsp;
me and so it's really what it's about and so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.240 --> 00:05:00.080
i think yeah i think if you're feeling like well&nbsp;
i want the money or i want the accolades it's just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:06.000
about getting really honest with yourself about&nbsp;
why you want those things everything that we say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.400
we want is because of how we think we're going to&nbsp;
feel when we get it so if you you know if you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:19.120
an oscar why why do what do you think you're going&nbsp;
to feel when you get that oscar and and i think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.520
that if you can break down those feelings it's&nbsp;
more important to sort of chase those feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:30.880
or to try to feel those now than necessarily the&nbsp;
the label that you think is going to give you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.760
those feelings um if that makes sense so i think&nbsp;
you know like i said in my book it's really about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:42.240
like set any goal that you want there's nothing&nbsp;
wrong with any of them um but if you're chasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.120
them for validation to make you feel good to&nbsp;
make you feel more worthy or more deserved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:55.920
deserved deserve it um it probably isn't going&nbsp;
to feel the way that you think it's going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.000
feel it's not going to solve the inner problem&nbsp;
right like none of the external things that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:06.880
create for ourselves or that we get aren't going&nbsp;
to are never going to solve an internal problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:13.520
i think most of this is is validation from&nbsp;
others or self-validation validation from others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.400
you think that matters more to most&nbsp;
people i think a lot i think a lot of us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:26.320
make decisions based on how others&nbsp;
will perceive it how like for example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.200
everyone and their mother in this industry says&nbsp;
that they want to work on netflix you know on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:38.160
netflix project and you know there might be some&nbsp;
like there might be some reasons behind that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:43.440
in the terms of well they do great work you know&nbsp;
they they tell complex stories and i'm interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:48.160
in the stories that they're telling but a lot of&nbsp;
people especially the actors that i work with or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:54.480
the directors the writers they say they want&nbsp;
netflix because netflix is a huge well-known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.480 --> 00:07:00.080
entity right now and if they book something&nbsp;
netflix they can then post it on social media&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:07.200
or they can tell people hey i booked a netflix&nbsp;
show and that makes them feel successful because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.240
they're perceived as successful because it's&nbsp;
a network or streamer that everybody knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.960
right but what if what was really important&nbsp;
to you that you booked a project that told a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:25.120
meaningful story that impacted people's lives and&nbsp;
that was really fun to create and it felt really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:28.320
great like you were working with great people&nbsp;
collaborating with great people and the whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:36.800
experience just felt good well what if you could&nbsp;
get that experience at abc or on hulu or you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:42.240
or another smaller now you know because i talk&nbsp;
about one of my best experiences in hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:47.920
was a show that was on abc family which is now&nbsp;
free form you know and i don't think many people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.040
are like i want to work on freeform like&nbsp;
everyone's like i want to work on netflix you know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:59.760
it's not maybe as sexy maybe they don't have quite&nbsp;
as many viewers but it was the most fun i ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:05.520
had on a show and we were telling a meaningful&nbsp;
story and there were really amazing crew and cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:13.280
members it was just a really good experience so&nbsp;
yeah i think that it's this is a long way to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:19.280
i i think it is about chasing validation from&nbsp;
others and how we are perceived by others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.160
and does that go back to sort of that&nbsp;
boxes thing that you said like being in la&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:29.680
you you think that there's these certain rules&nbsp;
in these boxes and it's the same thing about like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:37.280
oh oh you're just doing the um the score network&nbsp;
i've never heard of it yeah oh okay yeah no but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:43.920
if you were somewhere else oh wow you're on a tv&nbsp;
show how cool right but here there's these levels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:49.840
right the hierarchy yeah yeah i i don't know&nbsp;
if it's necessary i guess the box is in a way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:55.360
where you're like boxing yourself into what your&nbsp;
dream has to look like like my dream has to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:05.200
like me working for netflix um so i guess in a&nbsp;
way but i do think yeah that people don't realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:14.480
that it's probably going to be a more enjoyable&nbsp;
experience if you intentionally try to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.960
a good experience for yourself you know like&nbsp;
a show that you love working on that you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:23.440
doing meaningful work then whatever&nbsp;
the label of the network or the studio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:27.840
is you know because you know look like i've&nbsp;
i've known series regulars who have quit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.560
and who just like after a few seasons weren't&nbsp;
feeling fulfilled anymore it wasn't like a story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:38.640
they felt like was meaningful in their lives&nbsp;
you know and so that happens you know like you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.520
might get the thing that you think you want like&nbsp;
you might get netflix and then it not be a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.920
experience i'm not trying to put that out there&nbsp;
i'm sure like there's a lot of amazing experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:52.960
on netflix but my point is like get clear about&nbsp;
how you want the experience to feel and what you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:57.760
want the experience to look like like i say in&nbsp;
my book like write make a list of everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:02.240
that you want in the next project you want to&nbsp;
book or whatever goal you're working towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:07.040
write the list of everything that everything you&nbsp;
think netflix is going to give you right write&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:13.280
down everything you think it's going to give you&nbsp;
and then take away netflix at the top and then but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:18.720
still but still chase your list right so you're&nbsp;
still really going after what you truly want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:25.280
but you're allowing it to look however it looks&nbsp;
how do you help people with the part of success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:33.280
where they want what other people have i mean that&nbsp;
is happening all the time and i have found myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.280
getting caught up in that&nbsp;
too you know i think that

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.680
when people post things on social media i think&nbsp;
that's like really a lot of where it comes from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:49.840
as opposed to seeing it in actual real&nbsp;
life i think that when we see somebody's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.600
highlight reel on social media

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:58.400
we are putting a whole story behind that post&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:03.520
about what it means and how it must feel&nbsp;
for them to have what that thing right so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:11.120
if somebody posts a picture of themselves&nbsp;
driving a porsche you know a fan's very fancy car&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:17.520
and they're smiling in it and they're like yeah&nbsp;
you know they look cool you might then create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:23.920
this whole story about what that means for that&nbsp;
person and how their life must be so amazing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:28.720
it must feel so good for them and wow they have&nbsp;
so much money and we create this whole narrative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:34.640
about what it means when we see them having this&nbsp;
thing and we're like well we want those feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:42.640
i i want to feel financially stable i want to&nbsp;
feel wealthy i want to um feel excited about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:49.040
new purchase i want to have a car like that right&nbsp;
so we we think that they're feeling a certain way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:56.560
when they have something and then we want to feel&nbsp;
that way and so we think the way we feel it is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.560 --> 00:12:02.400
try to get the same thing they have and it's&nbsp;
so easy to get caught up in whatever we think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:09.920
you know people are or whatever we're seeing&nbsp;
people have you know even if it's a a booking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:13.600
you know if you book a job or you have an&nbsp;
audition or something you know i think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:21.760
if you see someone post online that um i'm&nbsp;
trying to think of something that maybe i've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:27.920
thought i wanted but i didn't actually want&nbsp;
like like for example one of my clients&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:31.920
said you know what they're an actor&nbsp;
and they were like you know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:37.760
every actor wants to be series regular they think&nbsp;
it's like hitting the lottery you know financial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:43.360
lottery because it's it's a lot of money and&nbsp;
it's consistent work and one of my clients was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.280
like you know what i don't think i want to be&nbsp;
serious regular at this time in my life like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:50.800
because you usually have to wake up at like four&nbsp;
in the morning you know you're there all day it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:54.800
a very long day you have to wake she's like i&nbsp;
don't know if i really i kind of like waking up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.800 --> 00:13:00.720
at eight o'clock and said you know i don't know if&nbsp;
that's really what i want in my life right now so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.840
she had to you know get honest about wait a minute&nbsp;
what makes me happy what would make me happy now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:13.360
so i think social media plays a big role in&nbsp;
it but but it's really what we decide it means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:19.840
right what we decide it means that this person&nbsp;
booked this project or has this opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:25.520
we also don't know the truth about what it means&nbsp;
to that person or what they're really feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:31.680
on the other side of it you know maybe they're&nbsp;
like posting i i had this amazing audition for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:37.680
this for netflix wow i'm so lucky i have such&nbsp;
a great life but really they're feeling like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:43.200
maybe it was like a two-line role and it was&nbsp;
something that they're not actually excited about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.600
but they're trying to tell the world that they had&nbsp;
this netflix audition and then people that see it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.600 --> 00:13:52.480
are like oh man they have this great life they're&nbsp;
getting these netflix auditions and then we create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:59.040
the story about what we think they're feeling&nbsp;
or what you know so i think it comes down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:04.560
what are the feelings you want to&nbsp;
feel when you get the thing you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:10.160
and stop assuming that every single&nbsp;
person who has something feels that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:15.840
exact way because i think we're attaching&nbsp;
those feelings to what other people have

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:35.280
you

